data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Take `u = log x` and `v = log y`. The slope is the covariance of `u` and `v` divided by the variance\nof `u`, both computed from the centred values. The intercept is the mean of `v` minus the slope\ntimes the mean of `u`. The coefficient `a` is `exp(intercept)`. Check the inputs first: same length,\nat least two points, one dimension, finite values, strictly positive values, and `x` not constant."},"hints_note":null}

